    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d410">

                <pb facs="0568" n="466" sameAs="frus:frus1919v01/pg466"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.51/2342</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Wallace</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-07-17"><hi rendition="#italic">July 17,
                            1919</hi></date>.<lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received July
                        31.</hi>]</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 252</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: In confirmation of my telegram No. 1098 of
                    yesterday’s date,<anchor n="39" xml:id="d410-f1"/> transmitting the reply of the
                    Minister for Foreign Affairs relative to the formula to be adopted as the
                    interpretation of the support which will be given by the American, French,
                    British and Japanese Governments, <pb facs="0569" n="467" xml:id="pg467"/> to
                    the agreement concluded on May 12th between the financial groups constituting
                    the new Consortium in China, I have the honor to enclose herewith copy and
                    translation of Mr. Pichon’s note.</p>
                <p>I have [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hugh C. Wallace</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d410-a1.xml" xpointer="d410-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
